        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ealdgyth, Sigeferth, Earngrim, Edmund II\n- Roles: wife, son, thegn, King of England\n- Places: Seven Burghs\n\nFacts:\n- Ealdgyth, whose modern English name may be Edith, lived circa 992 to after 1016.\n- Ealdgyth may have been the wife of Sigeferth.\n- Sigeferth was the son of Earngrim.\n- Sigeferth was a thegn of the Seven Burghs.\n- Ealdgyth later may have been the wife of Edmund II.\n- Edmund II was usually known as Edmund Ironside.\n- Edmund II was King of England from 23 April 1016 to 30 November 1016.",
